        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r167884580-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "Not as great as its publication..",
        "text": "I visited Pasupatinath on my way back to hotel in Thamel after visiting Bodnath. Taxi costs around Rs 200 from Bodnath to Pasupatinath, but you can also walk if you want to enjoy street scenery of Kathamandu. My taxi driver offered to guide me around temple for free if I took his cab back to the hotel, but once I pay the Rs 1000 entrance fee, one of the guide there told him to leave since only official guide is allowed. The guide insisted to use his service by telling me many spots inside the temple are holy and I need someone to guide my way through. Well, I do not have a choice. Inside, there's nothing much to see, no cremation, and only Sadhu are the main attraction. Plus point is the shelter for elderly accross the temple's main entrance, I was there to take some picture but end up talking with doctors from India who is doing voluntary work, really enlighting. Btw, I end up paying Rs 1000 to the guide :( so better negotiating the price upfront if you are followed by guide, and keep small rupee notes in your pocket.",
