        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r165932586-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "Considered the most holy temple of Shiva...",
        "text": "Located on the banks of the Bagmati River, the temple is just outside of Boudha in the outskirts of Kathmandu.  One can see devout Hindu pilgrims visiting the temple daily as well as funeral pyres of local and not so local Hindus.  The local Sadhus or Babas are very nice and interesting to talk to and will do their best to answer questions.  The Milk Baba is especially friendly and world famous.  Shivaratri, the annual celebration of Shiva is a crazy and jubilant event that is not to be missed if you are in the area.  All in all a worthwhile place to visit, and one of the few major Hindu temples that even allow non-Hindus inside.",
        "review_tip": null,
